#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid "A free IBM course on quantum information and computation"
msgstr "Isang libreng kurso ng IBM sa quantum information at computation"

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: sidebar_label
#, no-wrap
msgid "Discretization of errors"
msgstr "Discretization ng mga error"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"So far we've considered $X$ errors and $Z$ errors in the context of the 9-qubit Shor code, and in this section we'll consider arbitrary errors.\n"
"What we'll find is that, to handle such errors, we don't need to do anything different from what we've already discussed;\n"
"the ability to correct $X$ errors, $Z$ errors, or both, implies the ability to correct arbitrary errors.\n"
"This phenomenon is sometimes called the *discretization of errors*.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa ngayon, tinalakay na natin ang mga $X$ error at $Z$ error sa konteksto ng 9-qubit Shor code, at sa seksyong ito ay pag-aaralan natin ang mga arbitrary na error.\n"
"Mahahanap natin na, para harapin ang ganitong mga error, hindi na kailangan pang gumawa ng iba kaysa sa mga nabanggit na natin;\n"
"ang kakayahang i-correct ang mga $X$ error, $Z$ error, o pareho, ay nagbibigay ng kakayahang i-correct ang mga arbitrary na error.\n"
"Ang penomenong ito ay tinatawag minsan na *discretization ng mga error*.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Unitary qubit errors {#unitary-qubit-errors}"
msgstr "Mga unitary qubit error {#unitary-qubit-errors}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Let's begin with single-qubit *unitary* errors.\n"
"For example, such an error could correspond to a very small rotation of the Bloch sphere, possibly representing an error incurred by a gate that isn't perfect, for instance.\n"
"Or it could be any other unitary operation on a qubit and not necessarily one that's close to the identity.\n"
msgstr ""
"Magsimula tayo sa single-qubit na *unitary* na mga error.\n"
"Halimbawa, ang ganitong error ay maaaring kumatawan sa napakaliit na pag-ikot ng Bloch sphere, na posibleng nagpapakita ng error na dulot ng isang gate na hindi perpekto.\n"
"O maaari itong maging anumang iba pang unitary na operasyon sa isang qubit at hindi kailangang malapit sa identity.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"It might seem like correcting for such errors is difficult.\n"
"After all, there are infinitely many possible errors like this, and it's inconceivable that we could somehow identify each error exactly and then undo it.\n"
"However, as long as we can correct for a bit-flip, a phase-flip, or both, then we will succeed in correcting an arbitrary single-qubit unitary error using the procedures described earlier in the lesson.\n"
msgstr ""
"Maaaring mukhang mahirap ang pag-correct ng ganitong mga error.\n"
"Kung tutuusin, walang katapusang bilang ng posibleng ganitong mga error, at hindi makatotohanan na matukoy natin nang eksakto ang bawat error at bawiin ito.\n"
"Gayunpaman, basta maari tayong mag-correct ng bit-flip, phase-flip, o pareho, magtatagumpay tayo sa pag-correct ng anumang arbitrary na single-qubit unitary error gamit ang mga pamamaraang inilarawan kanina sa araling ito.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To see why this is the case, let us recognize first that we can express an "
"arbitrary $2 \\times 2$ unitary matrix $U,$ representing an error on a "
"single qubit, as a linear combination of the four Pauli matrices (including "
"the identity matrix).\n"
msgstr ""
"Para maintindihan kung bakit ganito, kailangan muna nating kilalanin na "
"maaari nating ipahayag ang anumang $2 \\times 2$ unitary matrix $U,$ na "
"kumakatawan sa isang error sa isang qubit, bilang linear combination ng apat"
" na Pauli matrices (kasama ang identity matrix).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"U = \\alpha \\mathbb{I} + \\beta X + \\gamma Y + \\delta Z\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"U = \\alpha \\mathbb{I} + \\beta X + \\gamma Y + \\delta Z\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"As we will see, when the error detection circuits are run, the measurements that give us the syndrome bits effectively collapse the state of the encoding probabilistically to one where an error (or lack of an error) represented by one of the four Pauli matrices has taken place.\n"
"(It follows from the fact that $U$ is unitary that the numbers $\\alpha,$ $\\beta,$ $\\gamma,$ and $\\delta$ must satisfy $\\vert\\alpha\\vert^2 + \\vert\\beta\\vert^2 + \\vert\\gamma\\vert^2 + \\vert\\delta\\vert^2 = 1,$\n"
"and indeed, the values $\\vert\\alpha\\vert^2,$ $\\vert\\beta\\vert^2,$ $\\vert\\gamma\\vert^2,$ and $\\vert\\delta\\vert^2$ are the probabilities with which the encoded state collapses to one for which the corresponding Pauli error has occurred.)\n"
msgstr ""
"Tulad ng makikita natin, kapag pinatakbo ang mga error detection circuit, ang mga measurement na nagbibigay sa atin ng syndrome bits ay epektibong nagko-collapse ng estado ng encoding nang probabilistiko sa isa kung saan naganap na ang isang error (o kawalan ng error) na kinakatawan ng isa sa apat na Pauli matrices.\n"
"(Sumusunod mula sa katotohanan na ang $U$ ay unitary na ang mga numerong $\\alpha,$ $\\beta,$ $\\gamma,$ at $\\delta$ ay dapat matugunan ang $\\vert\\alpha\\vert^2 + \\vert\\beta\\vert^2 + \\vert\\gamma\\vert^2 + \\vert\\delta\\vert^2 = 1,$\n"
"at sa katunayan, ang mga halagang $\\vert\\alpha\\vert^2,$ $\\vert\\beta\\vert^2,$ $\\vert\\gamma\\vert^2,$ at $\\vert\\delta\\vert^2$ ang mga probabilidad kung saan nagko-collapse ang encoded state sa isa kung saan naganap ang kaukulang Pauli error.)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To explain how this works in greater detail, it will be convenient to use subscripts to indicate which qubit a given qubit unitary operation acts upon.\n"
"For example, using Qiskit's qubit numbering convention $(\\mathsf{Q}_8,\\mathsf{Q}_7,\\ldots,\\mathsf{Q}_0)$ to number the 9 qubits used for the Shor code, we have these expressions for various unitary operations on single qubits, where in each case we tensor the unitary matrix with the identity matrix on every other qubit.\n"
msgstr ""
"Para ipaliwanag kung paano ito gumagana nang mas detalyado, magiging maginhawa ang paggamit ng mga subscript para ipakita kung aling qubit ang pinatatakbo ng isang partikular na qubit unitary operation.\n"
"Halimbawa, gamit ang Qiskit qubit numbering convention $(\\mathsf{Q}_8,\\mathsf{Q}_7,\\ldots,\\mathsf{Q}_0)$ para bilangan ang 9 na qubit na ginagamit para sa Shor code, mayroon tayong mga ekspresyong ito para sa iba't ibang unitary operations sa single qubits, kung saan sa bawat kaso ay ini-tensor natin ang unitary matrix sa identity matrix sa bawat ibang qubit.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"X_0 & = \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes X \\\\[1.5mm]\n"
"Z_4 & = \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes Z \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\\\[1.5mm]\n"
"U_7 & = \\mathbb{I} \\otimes U \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I}\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"X_0 & = \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes X \\\\[1.5mm]\n"
"Z_4 & = \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes Z \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\\\[1.5mm]\n"
"U_7 & = \\mathbb{I} \\otimes U \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I}\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"So, in particular, for a given qubit unitary operation $U,$ we can specify "
"the action of $U$ applied to qubit $k$ by the following formula, which is "
"similar to the one before except that each matrix represents an operation "
"applied to qubit $k.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Kaya, sa partikular, para sa isang partikular na qubit unitary operation "
"$U,$ maaari nating tukuyin ang aksyon ng $U$ na inilapat sa qubit $k$ sa "
"pamamagitan ng sumusunod na formula, na katulad ng nauna maliban na ang "
"bawat matrix ay kumakatawan sa operasyong inilapat sa qubit $k.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"U_k = \\alpha \\mathbb{I}_k + \\beta X_k + \\gamma Y_k + \\delta Z_k\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"U_k = \\alpha \\mathbb{I}_k + \\beta X_k + \\gamma Y_k + \\delta Z_k\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now suppose that $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ is the 9-qubit encoding of a qubit state.\n"
"If the error $U$ takes place on qubit $k,$ we obtain the state $U_k \\vert\\psi\\rangle,$ which can be expressed as a linear combination of Pauli operations acting on $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ as follows.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ngayon ipagpalagay na ang $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ ay ang 9-qubit encoding ng isang qubit state.\n"
"Kung ang error $U$ ay naganap sa qubit $k,$ makukuha natin ang estado $U_k \\vert\\psi\\rangle,$ na maaaring ipahayag bilang linear combination ng mga Pauli operations na kumikilos sa $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ tulad ng sumusunod.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"U_k \\vert\\psi\\rangle = \\alpha \\vert\\psi\\rangle + \\beta X_k\\vert\\psi\\rangle + \\gamma Y_k\\vert\\psi\\rangle + \\delta Z_k\\vert\\psi\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"U_k \\vert\\psi\\rangle = \\alpha \\vert\\psi\\rangle + \\beta X_k\\vert\\psi\\rangle + \\gamma Y_k\\vert\\psi\\rangle + \\delta Z_k\\vert\\psi\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "At this point let's make the substitution $Y = iXZ.$\n"
msgstr "Sa puntong ito, gawin natin ang substitusyon na $Y = iXZ.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"U_k \\vert\\psi\\rangle = \\alpha \\vert\\psi\\rangle + \\beta X_k\\vert\\psi\\rangle + i \\gamma X_kZ_k\\vert\\psi\\rangle + \\delta Z_k\\vert\\psi\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"U_k \\vert\\psi\\rangle = \\alpha \\vert\\psi\\rangle + \\beta X_k\\vert\\psi\\rangle + i \\gamma X_kZ_k\\vert\\psi\\rangle + \\delta Z_k\\vert\\psi\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now consider the error-detection and correction steps described previously.\n"
"We can think about the measurement outcomes for the three inner code parity checks along with the one for the outer code collectively as a single syndrome consisting of 8 bits.\n"
"Just prior to the actual standard basis measurements that produce these syndrome bits, the state has the following form.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ngayon isaalang-alang ang mga hakbang ng error-detection at correction na inilarawan kanina.\n"
"Maaari nating isipin ang mga measurement outcome para sa tatlong inner code parity checks kasama ang isa para sa outer code nang sama-sama bilang isang syndrome na binubuo ng 8 bits.\n"
"Bago pa man ang aktwal na standard basis measurements na gumagawa ng mga syndrome bits na ito, ang estado ay may sumusunod na anyo.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{gathered}\n"
"\\alpha\\,\\vert \\mathbb{I} \\text{ syndrome}\\rangle \\otimes \\vert\\psi\\rangle \\\\\n"
"+ \\beta\\,\\vert X_k \\text{ syndrome}\\rangle \\otimes X_k\\vert\\psi\\rangle \\\\\n"
"+ i \\gamma\\,\\vert X_k Z_k \\text{ syndrome}\\rangle \\otimes X_k Z_k\\vert\\psi\\rangle \\\\\n"
"+ \\delta\\,\\vert Z_k \\text{ syndrome}\\rangle \\otimes Z_k\\vert\\psi\\rangle\n"
"\\end{gathered}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{gathered}\n"
"\\alpha\\,\\vert \\mathbb{I} \\text{ syndrome}\\rangle \\otimes \\vert\\psi\\rangle \\\\\n"
"+ \\beta\\,\\vert X_k \\text{ syndrome}\\rangle \\otimes X_k\\vert\\psi\\rangle \\\\\n"
"+ i \\gamma\\,\\vert X_k Z_k \\text{ syndrome}\\rangle \\otimes X_k Z_k\\vert\\psi\\rangle \\\\\n"
"+ \\delta\\,\\vert Z_k \\text{ syndrome}\\rangle \\otimes Z_k\\vert\\psi\\rangle\n"
"\\end{gathered}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To be clear, we have two systems at this point.\n"
"The system on the left is the 8 qubits we'll measure to get the syndrome, where $\\vert \\mathbb{I} \\text{ syndrome}\\rangle,$\n"
"$\\vert X_k \\text{ syndrome}\\rangle,$ and so on, refer to whatever 8-qubit standard basis state is consistent with the corresponding error (or non-error).\n"
"The system on the right is the 9 qubits we're using for the encoding.\n"
msgstr ""
"Para maging malinaw, mayroon na tayong dalawang sistema sa puntong ito.\n"
"Ang sistema sa kaliwa ay ang 8 qubits na susukatin natin para makuha ang syndrome, kung saan ang $\\vert \\mathbb{I} \\text{ syndrome}\\rangle,$\n"
"$\\vert X_k \\text{ syndrome}\\rangle,$ at iba pa, ay tumutukoy sa anumang 8-qubit standard basis state na naaayon sa kaukulang error (o kawalan ng error).\n"
"Ang sistema sa kanan ay ang 9 qubits na ginagamit natin para sa encoding.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Notice that these two systems are now correlated (in general), and this is the key to why this works.\n"
"By measuring the syndrome, the state of the 9 qubits on the right effectively collapses to one in which a Pauli error consistent with the measured syndrome has been applied to one of the qubits.\n"
"Moreover, the syndrome itself provides enough information so that we can undo the error and recover the original encoding $\\vert\\psi\\rangle.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Pansinin na ang dalawang sistemang ito ay magkaugnay na ngayon (sa pangkalahatan), at ito ang susi kung bakit ito gumagana.\n"
"Sa pag-sukat ng syndrome, ang estado ng 9 qubits sa kanan ay epektibong nagco-collapse sa isa kung saan ang isang Pauli error na naaayon sa nasukat na syndrome ay nailapat sa isa sa mga qubit.\n"
"Bukod dito, ang syndrome mismo ay nagbibigay ng sapat na impormasyon para mabawi natin ang error at maibalik ang orihinal na encoding $\\vert\\psi\\rangle.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In particular, if the syndrome qubits are measured and the appropriate "
"corrections are made, we obtain a state that can be expressed as a density "
"matrix,\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa partikular, kung ang mga syndrome qubit ay nasukat at ang mga angkop na "
"correction ay ginawa, makukuha natin ang isang estado na maaaring ipahayag "
"bilang density matrix,\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\xi \\otimes \\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\xi \\otimes \\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert,\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "where\n"
msgstr "kung saan\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\xi = & \\vert\\alpha\\vert^2 \\vert \\mathbb{I} \\text{ syndrome}\\rangle\\langle \\mathbb{I} \\text{ syndrome}\\vert \\\\[1mm]\n"
"& + \\vert\\beta\\vert^2 \\vert X_k \\text{ syndrome}\\rangle\\langle X_k \\text{ syndrome}\\vert\\\\[1mm]\n"
"& + \\vert\\gamma\\vert^2 \\vert X_k Z_k \\text{ syndrome}\\rangle\\langle X_k Z_k \\text{ syndrome}\\vert\\\\[1mm]\n"
"& + \\vert\\delta\\vert^2 \\vert Z_k \\text{ syndrome}\\rangle\\langle Z_k \\text{ syndrome}\\vert.\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\xi = & \\vert\\alpha\\vert^2 \\vert \\mathbb{I} \\text{ syndrome}\\rangle\\langle \\mathbb{I} \\text{ syndrome}\\vert \\\\[1mm]\n"
"& + \\vert\\beta\\vert^2 \\vert X_k \\text{ syndrome}\\rangle\\langle X_k \\text{ syndrome}\\vert\\\\[1mm]\n"
"& + \\vert\\gamma\\vert^2 \\vert X_k Z_k \\text{ syndrome}\\rangle\\langle X_k Z_k \\text{ syndrome}\\vert\\\\[1mm]\n"
"& + \\vert\\delta\\vert^2 \\vert Z_k \\text{ syndrome}\\rangle\\langle Z_k \\text{ syndrome}\\vert.\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Critically, this is a product state:\n"
"we have our original, uncorrupted encoding as the right-hand tensor factor,\n"
"and on the left we have a density matrix $\\xi$ that describes a random error syndrome.\n"
"There is no longer any correlation with the system on the right, which is the one we care about, because the errors have been corrected.\n"
"At this point we can throw the syndrome qubits away or reset them so we can use them again.\n"
"This is how the randomness — or *entropy* — created by errors is removed from the system.\n"
msgstr ""
"Mahalaga, ito ay isang product state:\n"
"mayroon tayong orihinal, hindi nasirang encoding bilang right-hand tensor factor,\n"
"at sa kaliwa ay mayroon tayong density matrix $\\xi$ na naglalarawan ng random na error syndrome.\n"
"Wala nang ugnayan sa sistema sa kanan, na siyang pinagmamalasakitan natin, dahil naitama na ang mga error.\n"
"Sa puntong ito maaari na nating itapon ang mga syndrome qubit o i-reset ang mga ito para magamit muli.\n"
"Ganito ang pag-aalis ng randomness — o *entropy* — na nilikha ng mga error mula sa sistema.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This is the discretization of errors for the special case of unitary errors.\n"
"In essence, by measuring the syndrome, we effectively *project* the error onto an error that's described by a Pauli matrix.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ito ang discretization ng mga error para sa espesyal na kaso ng mga unitary error.\n"
"Sa esensya, sa pag-sukat ng syndrome, epektibong *ini-project* natin ang error sa isang error na inilarawan ng isang Pauli matrix.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"At first glance it may seem too good to be true that we can correct for arbitrary unitary errors like this, even errors that are tiny and hardly noticeable on their own.\n"
"But, what's important to realize here is that this is a unitary error on a *single* qubit, and by the design of the code, a single-qubit operation can't change the state of the logical qubit that's been encoded.\n"
"All it can possibly do is to move the state out of the subspace of valid encodings, but then the error detections collapse the state and the corrections bring it back to where it started.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa unang tingin, maaaring mukhang masyadong maganda para maging totoo na maaari nating i-correct ang mga arbitrary na unitary error tulad nito, kahit na ang mga error na napakaliit at halos hindi kapansin-pansin sa kanilang sarili.\n"
"Ngunit, ang mahalagang maunawaan dito ay ito ay isang unitary error sa isang *single* na qubit, at sa disenyo ng code, ang isang single-qubit na operasyon ay hindi maaaring baguhin ang estado ng logical qubit na na-encode.\n"
"Ang kaya nitong gawin ay ilipat ang estado mula sa subspace ng mga valid na encoding, ngunit pagkatapos ang mga error detection ay nagco-collapse ng estado at ang mga correction ay nagbabalik nito sa dati.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Arbitrary qubit errors {#arbitrary-qubit-errors}"
msgstr "Mga arbitrary na qubit error {#arbitrary-qubit-errors}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Finally, let's consider arbitrary errors that are not necessarily unitary.\n"
"To be precise, we'll consider an error described by an arbitrary qubit channel $\\Phi.$\n"
"For example, this could be a dephasing or depolarizing channel, a reset channel, or a strange channel that we've never thought about before.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa wakas, isaalang-alang natin ang mga arbitrary na error na hindi kailangang unitary.\n"
"Sa katumpakan, isasaalang-alang natin ang isang error na inilarawan ng isang arbitrary na qubit channel $\\Phi.$\n"
"Halimbawa, ito ay maaaring isang dephasing o depolarizing channel, isang reset channel, o isang kakaibang channel na hindi pa natin naiisip noon.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The first step is to consider any Kraus representation of $\\Phi.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang unang hakbang ay isaalang-alang ang anumang Kraus representation ng "
"$\\Phi.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\Phi(\\sigma) = \\sum_j A_j \\sigma A_j^{\\dagger}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\Phi(\\sigma) = \\sum_j A_j \\sigma A_j^{\\dagger}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This is a qubit channel, so each $A_j$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix, which we "
"can express as a linear combination of Pauli matrices.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ito ay isang qubit channel, kaya ang bawat $A_j$ ay isang $2\\times 2$ "
"matrix, na maaari nating ipahayag bilang linear combination ng mga Pauli "
"matrices.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"A_j = \\alpha_j \\mathbb{I} + \\beta_j X + \\gamma_j Y + \\delta_j Z\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"A_j = \\alpha_j \\mathbb{I} + \\beta_j X + \\gamma_j Y + \\delta_j Z\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This allows us to express the action of the error $\\Phi$ on a chosen qubit "
"$k$ in terms of Pauli matrices as follows.\n"
msgstr ""
"Nagbibigay-daan ito sa atin na ipahayag ang aksyon ng error na $\\Phi$ sa "
"isang piniling qubit $k$ sa pamamagitan ng mga Pauli matrices tulad ng "
"sumusunod.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\Phi_k \\bigl( \\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert\\bigr) =\n"
"\\sum_j (\\alpha_j \\mathbb{I}_k + \\beta_j X_k + \\gamma_j Y_k + \\delta_j Z_k) \\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert\n"
"(\\alpha_j \\mathbb{I}_k + \\beta_j X_k + \\gamma_j Y_k + \\delta_j Z_k)^{\\dagger}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\Phi_k \\bigl( \\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert\\bigr) =\n"
"\\sum_j (\\alpha_j \\mathbb{I}_k + \\beta_j X_k + \\gamma_j Y_k + \\delta_j Z_k) \\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert\n"
"(\\alpha_j \\mathbb{I}_k + \\beta_j X_k + \\gamma_j Y_k + \\delta_j Z_k)^{\\dagger}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In short, we've simply expanded out all of our Kraus matrices as linear "
"combinations of Pauli matrices.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa madaling salita, pinalawak lang natin ang lahat ng ating Kraus matrices "
"bilang mga linear combination ng Pauli matrices.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If we now compute and measure the error syndrome, and correct for any errors"
" that are revealed, we'll obtain a similar sort of state to what we had in "
"the case of a unitary error:\n"
msgstr ""
"Kung ngayon ay kinukuha at sinusukat natin ang error syndrome, at ini-"
"correct ang mga error na naihayag, makakakuha tayo ng katulad na uri ng "
"estado tulad ng nasa kaso ng unitary error:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "where this time we have\n"
msgstr "kung saan sa pagkakataong ito mayroon tayong\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\xi = & \\sum_j \\Bigl(\\vert\\alpha_j\\vert^2 \\vert \\mathbb{I} \\text{ syndrome}\\rangle\\langle \\mathbb{I} \\text{ syndrome}\\vert \\\\[-3mm]\n"
"& \\qquad + \\vert\\beta_j\\vert^2 \\vert X_k \\text{ syndrome}\\rangle\\langle X_k \\text{ syndrome}\\vert\\\\[2mm]\n"
"& \\qquad + \\vert\\gamma_j\\vert^2 \\vert X_k Z_k \\text{ syndrome}\\rangle\\langle X_k Z_k \\text{ syndrome}\\vert\\\\[2mm]\n"
"& \\qquad + \\vert\\delta_j\\vert^2 \\vert Z_k \\text{ syndrome}\\rangle\\langle Z_k \\text{ syndrome}\\vert \\Bigr).\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\xi = & \\sum_j \\Bigl(\\vert\\alpha_j\\vert^2 \\vert \\mathbb{I} \\text{ syndrome}\\rangle\\langle \\mathbb{I} \\text{ syndrome}\\vert \\\\[-3mm]\n"
"& \\qquad + \\vert\\beta_j\\vert^2 \\vert X_k \\text{ syndrome}\\rangle\\langle X_k \\text{ syndrome}\\vert\\\\[2mm]\n"
"& \\qquad + \\vert\\gamma_j\\vert^2 \\vert X_k Z_k \\text{ syndrome}\\rangle\\langle X_k Z_k \\text{ syndrome}\\vert\\\\[2mm]\n"
"& \\qquad + \\vert\\delta_j\\vert^2 \\vert Z_k \\text{ syndrome}\\rangle\\langle Z_k \\text{ syndrome}\\vert \\Bigr).\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The details are a bit messier and are not shown here.\n"
"Conceptually speaking, the idea is identical to the unitary case.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang mga detalye ay medyo mas kumplikado at hindi ipinapakita dito.\n"
"Sa konsepto, ang ideya ay kapareho ng unitary na kaso.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Generalization {#generalization}"
msgstr "Generalization {#generalization}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The discretization of errors generalizes to other quantum error-correcting codes, including ones that can detect and correct errors on multiple qubits.\n"
"In such cases, errors on multiple qubits can be expressed as *tensor products* of Pauli matrices, and correspondingly different syndromes specify Pauli operation corrections that might be performed on multiple qubits rather than just one qubit.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang discretization ng mga error ay nagge-generalize sa ibang mga quantum error-correcting code, kasama na ang mga maaaring makatuklas at makapag-correct ng mga error sa maraming qubit.\n"
"Sa ganitong mga kaso, ang mga error sa maraming qubit ay maaaring ipahayag bilang mga *tensor products* ng mga Pauli matrices, at naaayon na ang iba't ibang syndrome ay nagtatakda ng mga Pauli operation corrections na maaaring isagawa sa maraming qubit sa halip na isang qubit lamang.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Again, by measuring the syndrome, errors are effectively projected or collapsed onto a discrete set of possibilities represented by tensor products of Pauli matrices, and by correcting for those Pauli errors, we can recover the original encoded state.\n"
"Meanwhile, whatever randomness is generated in the process is moved into the syndrome qubits, which are discarded or reset, thereby removing the randomness generated in this process from the system that stores the encoding.\n"
msgstr ""
"Muli, sa pag-sukat ng syndrome, ang mga error ay epektibong na-project o na-collapse sa isang discrete na hanay ng mga posibilidad na kinakatawan ng mga tensor products ng mga Pauli matrices, at sa pag-correct ng mga Pauli error na iyon, mababawi natin ang orihinal na encoded state.\n"
"Samantala, anumang randomness na nalilikha sa proseso ay inililipat sa mga syndrome qubit, na itinatapon o niri-reset, kaya tinatanggal ang randomness na nalilikha sa prosesong ito mula sa sistema na nag-iimbak ng encoding.\n"
